CRITICAL CONTINUITY RULES — follow exactly:
- DO NOT move any character to a different side of the frame. A character on the left of the reference image MUST remain on the left. A character on the right MUST remain on the right. Never swap their positions.
- DO NOT flip or mirror any character's facing direction. If a character faces screen-right in the reference, they face screen-right here too.
- DO NOT cross the 180-degree line. The camera stays on the same side of the action as the reference; only its angle and distance change.
- DO NOT alter character identity, wardrobe, hair, skin tone, or physical features — match the reference exactly.
- DO NOT change the setting, time of day, or lighting mood — this is the same scene, a new angle.
- Expressions, gestures, and body poses MAY evolve to match the current action. Screen positions and facing directions MAY NOT.
- Subtle film grain, cinematic color grading.
